---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/common/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/common/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Iteron | Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for Iteron by Turing Club, IISER Mohali."
>
  <Navbar />

  <main class="page-container">
    <header class="header-box brutalist-block">
      <h1 class="glitch" data-text="PRIVACY POLICY">PRIVACY POLICY</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">> EFFECTIVE DATE: 6 APRIL 2026 | LAST UPDATED: 6 APRIL 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how Iteron (operated by Turing Club, IISER Mohali and its
        core organizers listed on the About page) handles personal information related to this
        website and tournament workflow.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>1. Data Controller and Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For purposes of this Platform, Turing Club, IISER Mohali (through its designated core
        organizers) acts as the primary controller of personal data described in this policy.
        Contact: <a href="mailto:iteron.iiserm@gmail.com">iteron.iiserm@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>2. Data We May Collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Identity/contact data you provide in forms (for example: name, email, institution, submission details).</li>
        <li>Submission data required for tournament administration and publication workflows.</li>
        <li>
          We do not intentionally collect analytics telemetry, browser profiling/fingerprinting data,
          or advertising-tracking data for this Platform.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>3. How We Use Data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To receive, evaluate, and administer strategy submissions.</li>
        <li>To communicate updates related to participation, tournament logistics, and results.</li>
        <li>To publish public submissions/results as described in the Terms of Use.</li>
        <li>To maintain platform reliability, safety, and policy enforcement.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>4. Legal Bases for Processing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Consent, where you provide information voluntarily and agree to policy terms.</li>
        <li>Performance of tournament administration and related participant communications.</li>
        <li>Legitimate interests, including platform integrity, security, dispute handling, and publication workflows.</li>
        <li>Compliance with legal obligations, where applicable.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>5. Public vs Private Information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          By default, publicly released participant information is limited to strategy content,
          creator identification, and institute/affiliation details.
        </li>
        <li>
          Personal contact details (including email and equivalent contact fields) are not intended
          to be publicly published.
        </li>
        <li>
          If a participant requests anonymized or alternative public attribution, organizers may honor
          that request on receipt of a valid reason and after reasonable review.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>6. Third-Party Services and Data Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        Submission workflows may involve third-party form-processing services. Those services process data
        under their own privacy terms.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>We may share data with service providers that support forms, communications, and hosting.</li>
        <li>We may disclose data when required by law, legal process, or to protect rights, safety, and platform integrity.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>7. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
      <p>
        This Platform does not intentionally deploy analytics or advertising cookies.
        Any strictly necessary technical storage used by core site functionality is limited to
        operational purposes only.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>8. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain information for as long as necessary to run tournament operations, maintain archives,
        fulfill legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce policies.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Submission and tournament-operation data may be retained for up to 5 years after the relevant tournament cycle.</li>
        <li>Publicly released research archives may be retained for historical and academic continuity.</li>
        <li>Where deletion is requested and legally applicable, we will process deletion within reasonable operational timelines.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>9. Data Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable administrative and technical safeguards, but no system can be guaranteed fully secure.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>10. International Access and Transfers</h2>
      <p>
        The Platform may be accessed from multiple jurisdictions. Where data is processed across borders,
        we aim to apply reasonable safeguards consistent with applicable law and operational necessity.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>11. Your Rights and Requests</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on applicable law, you may request access, correction, or deletion of personal data.
        Send requests to <a href="mailto:iteron.iiserm@gmail.com">iteron.iiserm@gmail.com</a> with
        subject line "Privacy Request".
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>We target acknowledgment of requests within 7 calendar days.</li>
        <li>We target substantive response within 30 calendar days, subject to complexity and legal constraints.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>12. Children</h2>
      <p>
        The Platform is not intended for children below the age where independent consent is not legally valid
        in your jurisdiction.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>13. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy. The "Last Updated" date will be revised when changes are published.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-card brutalist-block">
      <h2>14. Contact and Grievance</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy contact: <a href="mailto:iteron.iiserm@gmail.com">iteron.iiserm@gmail.com</a>.
        If your concern is unresolved, you may escalate to
        <a href="mailto:turingclub@iisermohali.ac.in">turingclub@iisermohali.ac.in</a>
        with subject line "Privacy Escalation".
      </p>
      <p>
        For anonymity/attribution requests before publication, email
        <a href="mailto:iteron.iiserm@gmail.com">iteron.iiserm@gmail.com</a>
        with subject line "Attribution Request" and include your submission identifier and reason.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-container {
    padding: 120px 5% 5rem;
    max-width: 980px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    min-height: 100vh;
  }

  .header-box {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
    border-color: var(--accent-purple);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2.8rem;
    color: var(--text-white);
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    letter-spacing: 3px;
  }

  .subtitle {
    color: var(--accent-purple);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: bold;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
  }

  .legal-card {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    border-color: var(--text-white);
  }

  .legal-card h2 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }

  .legal-card p,
  .legal-card li {
    color: #cfcfcf;
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .legal-card ul {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .legal-card li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }

  .legal-card li::before {
    content: ">";
    color: var(--accent-purple);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .page-container {
      padding: 110px 1.25rem 3.5rem;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 2rem;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    h1 {
      font-size: 1.45rem;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
    }

    .subtitle {
      font-size: 0.84rem;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
    }
  }
</style>
